{"archetypes":[{"name":"ci-propagation","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks whether removing lint-bash32 from the make lint umbrella truly has no CI coverage gap, given the claimed propagation path through pre-commit run --all-files.","prompt_body":"The plan removes lint-bash32 from the make lint umbrella (line 23) on the premise that CI's make lint-only → pre-commit run --all-files covers it. Verify in .github/workflows/ci.yaml and the Makefile that this propagation chain is unbroken and that pre-commit run --all-files actually runs the hook against all repo shell files (not only staged ones). Check whether any CI job calls make lint directly (bypassing lint-only) or calls make lint-bash32 as a separate step that would become redundant or absent after the edit. Confirm the plan's Approach section's propagation claim is grounded in the actual workflow file, not assumed. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"doc-sync","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks whether docs/linting.md (canonical per AGENTS.md) needs updating for the Makefile umbrella change and new pre-commit hook, since the plan only adds updates to lint-bash32.md.","prompt_body":"AGENTS.md names docs/linting.md as the canonical source for linters and Makefile targets. The plan modifies the make lint umbrella and adds a new pre-commit hook but lists only scripts/lint-bash32.md for doc updates. Read docs/linting.md to determine whether it documents the lint: umbrella dependency list, the lint-bash32 target, or the pre-commit hook inventory, and flag any content that would be stale after the plan is applied. Also check if README.md or docs/configuration-and-permissions.md reference the lint umbrella in a way that becomes misleading. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-inc-bash","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's Failure modes section identifies a missing .inc.bash positional test as a risk, but the UPDATED: test file section only specifies three .sh-centric cases, leaving the coverage gap unresolved.","prompt_body":"The plan's Failure modes section (item 1) states that an .inc.bash positional case should be included in test-lint-bash32.sh to validate the files: regex in .pre-commit-config.yaml. However, the UPDATED: scripts/test-lint-bash32.sh section enumerates exactly three new cases, none of which targets .inc.bash. Verify whether the existing good.sh / bad-unsuppressed.sh fixtures in the test harness already cover .inc.bash paths, or whether this is an unresolved gap between the stated mitigation and the specified test additions. Also check whether the positional non-shell-path test (case 3) would catch a misconfigured files: regex, or whether that requires a dedicated .inc.bash fixture invoked positionally. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
